{% comment %}
================================================================================
CART WEBHOOK ADDITION — id_rec_category_l2
================================================================================
PURPOSE: Add `id_rec_category_l2` to the existing Cart Viewed webhook output.
         This attribute is the unified "what to recommend" signal. For cart, it
         is the L2 category of the highest-value item in the cart (already
         computed as `top_cat_clean` by the existing webhook logic).

WHERE TO ADD: Paste the Liquid below at the very end of the existing Cart Viewed
              webhook, immediately before the final closing `}` of the attributes
              JSON object. The existing webhook already computes `top_cat_clean`
              (e.g. "Furniture > Sofas") — this addition reads that variable and
              writes the L2 slice as a new attribute.

EXAMPLE:
  top_cat_clean = "Furniture > Sofas"       → id_rec_category_l2 = "Sofas"
  top_cat_clean = "Furniture > Sectionals > Corner Sectionals"
                                             → id_rec_category_l2 = "Sectionals"
  top_cat_clean = "Rugs"                    → id_rec_category_l2 = "Rugs"

HOW IT WORKS:
  Split on " > " and take index [1] (the L2 segment). If there is no " > "
  (i.e. top_cat_clean is already a bare category like "Rugs"), index [1] is nil,
  so we default to index [0] (the whole string).

ATTRIBUTE WRITTEN: `id_rec_category_l2` (STRING) on the Braze user profile.
  This overwrites any previous value — most recent cart event wins automatically.
  Browse abandon, batch, and post-purchase canvases also write this attribute;
  the most recently fired canvas's value is always current.
================================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %} ── Extract L2 from top_cat_clean ─────────────────────────────── {% endcomment %}
{% assign top_cat_parts  = top_cat_clean | split: ' > ' %}
{% assign top_cat_l2     = top_cat_parts[1] | default: top_cat_parts[0] | default: '' %}

{% comment %}
  Add the following key–value pair to the existing attributes JSON object,
  just before the closing brace.  Example of the insertion point:

      "cart_products": {{ cart_products_json }},
      "id_rec_category_l2": "{{ top_cat_l2 | replace: '"','' }}"   ← ADD THIS
    }
  ]
}

  Note: the replace filter strips any embedded quotes that could break JSON.
{% endcomment %}
